WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.361 --> 00:00:15.844
The new kittens were soon hidden safely with the others, thanks to Sebastian.

2
00:00:16.404 --> 00:00:21.787
For the second day now, Clara's lesson had been interrupted with laughter and excitement.

3
00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:25.729
Later in the day, everything was explained to Fraulein.

4
00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:32.729
She quickly realized that Heidi's trip the day before was the cause of all the chaos.

5
00:00:32.749 --> 00:00:38.531
"I am going to punish you for all your bad behavior," she told Heidi.

6
00:00:38.551 --> 00:00:42.193
"I'll put you in the cellar with the rats and black beetles."

7
00:00:43.753 --> 00:00:45.294
Heidi was silent and puzzled.

8
00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:50.596
She did not know what a cellar was like, and she had never seen a rat or a

9
00:00:50.696 --> 00:00:51.356
black beetle.

10
00:00:52.037 --> 00:00:54.297
But Clara interrupted in great distress.

11
00:00:55.678 --> 00:01:02.328
Clara's father had written to say that he would be home soon, so she said, "No, no, Fraulein,

12
00:01:02.769 --> 00:01:04.689
you must wait until Father arrives.

13
00:01:05.289 --> 00:01:07.410
He will say what is to be done with Heidi."

14
00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:13.351
"Fine, Clara, but I will have something to say to Herr Sesemann when he arrives!"

15
00:01:14.212 --> 00:01:15.272
replied Fraulein.

16
00:01:16.792 --> 00:01:19.673
The next days went by without any further disturbance.

17
00:01:20.373 --> 00:01:22.714
Heidi and Clara did their lessons in the mornings.

18
00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:30.892
In the afternoons, Heidi told Clara about Grandfather's hut on the mountain, about Peter and the goats, and

19
00:01:30.972 --> 00:01:31.773
Peter's Grannie.

20
00:01:33.374 --> 00:01:35.415
Heidi's heart was longing to return.

21
00:01:36.115 --> 00:01:39.757
She would always finish her stories with, "I must go home!

22
00:01:40.217 --> 00:01:42.239
Tomorrow I must really go home!"

23
00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:49.463
Even though Heidi missed her old home, she had a secret that cheered her up a little every

24
00:01:49.503 --> 00:01:56.086
day. She knew how much Peter's grandmother would love the soft white rolls that were served with dinner.

25
00:01:56.767 --> 00:02:01.862
So after each meal, she pocketed a roll and saved it in her room.

26
00:02:03.483 --> 00:02:09.766
Detie had told her that she could go home any time she wanted, and one morning Heidi decided

27
00:02:09.866 --> 00:02:11.147
she could stay no longer.

28
00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:18.150
From the bundle of clothes Detie had brought to Frankfurt, Heidi chose her red shawl and straw hat.

29
00:02:19.791 --> 00:02:23.914
She tied up the rolls in her shawl and put the hat on her head.

30
00:02:24.574 --> 00:02:28.036
Just as she reached the front door, she ran into Fraulein.

31
00:02:28.888 --> 00:02:30.209
"What are you doing?

32
00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:33.412
Have I not strictly forbidden you to run about?"

33
00:02:34.052 --> 00:02:34.833
said Fraulein.

34
00:02:34.853 --> 00:02:37.475
"I am not going to run about.

35
00:02:37.955 --> 00:02:38.896
I am going home!"

36
00:02:39.416 --> 00:02:42.739
said Heidi, hiding the bundle of rolls behind her back.

37
00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:44.821
"What are you talking about?

38
00:02:45.221 --> 00:02:47.002
Have you not been treated well here?

39
00:02:47.643 --> 00:02:49.344
What would Clara's father say?"

40
00:02:50.105 --> 00:02:50.845
said Fraulein.

41
00:02:50.865 --> 00:02:53.688
"But I only want to go home.

42
00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:55.901
Grannie is waiting for me.

43
00:02:55.921 --> 00:02:58.202
I can't share my lunch with Peter.

44
00:02:58.222 --> 00:03:01.263
And I can't watch the sunset on the mountains!"

45
00:03:01.963 --> 00:03:02.803
exclaimed Heidi.

46
00:03:03.484 --> 00:03:05.464
"The child is out of her mind!"

47
00:03:05.965 --> 00:03:06.905
cried Fraulein.

48
00:03:08.586 --> 00:03:13.388
She grabbed Heidi's hand, took away her hat and shawl, and gave them to Sebastian.

49
00:03:13.408 --> 00:03:17.749
"Take her to her room at once," said Fraulein.

50
00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:21.151
Heidi climbed the stairs with slow, heavy steps.

51
00:03:21.831 --> 00:03:24.092
Sebastian felt sad as he watched her.

52
00:03:24.684 --> 00:03:25.325
"Don't give in!"

53
00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:26.245
he said.

54
00:03:26.265 --> 00:03:28.327
"Don't let her make you unhappy!

55
00:03:28.967 --> 00:03:29.928
Keep up your courage!"

56
00:03:31.369 --> 00:03:37.013
Later in the day, Fraulein remembered what Heidi had been wearing when she had tried to leave.

57
00:03:37.713 --> 00:03:41.256
She decided to add some of Clara's clothes to Heidi's wardrobe.

58
00:03:41.736 --> 00:03:45.439
When she opened Heidi's closet, she couldn't believe what she saw.

59
00:03:45.459 --> 00:03:48.721
"What is this, Heidi?

60
00:03:49.321 --> 00:03:52.584
A pile of old rolls in the bottom of your closet?!"

61
00:03:53.216 --> 00:03:54.618
Fraulein called Sebastian.

62
00:03:54.638 --> 00:03:57.682
"Take away these old rolls at once!"

63
00:03:58.483 --> 00:03:59.324
ordered Fraulein.

64
00:03:59.344 --> 00:04:01.627
"No, no!"

65
00:04:02.448 --> 00:04:03.248
screamed Heidi.

66
00:04:03.269 --> 00:04:05.331
"The rolls are for Grannie!"

67
00:04:06.092 --> 00:04:10.958
But Fraulein would not listen, and Heidi flung herself down on her bed in despair.
